Every original evidence file, including raw process times, terminal observations, stderr/stdout and wire data, is copied byte-for-byte. JSON is parsed for checking but original evidence is not re-encoded. Gzip is allowed only for explicitly listed, byte-identical before/final pairs, with filename empty, mtime zero and level 9. Full two-source decompression and repeated-encoding equality are future mandatory checks; no gzip was produced here. Uncombined pairs retain both raw originals.

The future intake membership is N−G+14, where N is the final original-version row count and G is the number of explicitly validated equal bookend pairs. Fourteen fixed automatic paths cover progress, its raw preimage, eight preparation records, history proof, seal map, archive index and manifest. A separate staging preparation-review.json is outside the intake target count. The exact sorted target list must be supplied by Root and match before any physical write.

